{
 "_about": [
  "The phone frames the Windows mirror window (windows/PhoneUseMirror: PhoneModel.cs, FrameFinish.cs) and the browser mirror (index.html) draw. One table for both.",
  "frame: the band's width and the side buttons' room, in units of the screen's short side.",
  "models: by the model identifier AirPlay reports. glass: the black border between screen and band, in units of the screen's width (1.2 mm on the 16 Pro and 1.71 mm on the 15 Pro, reported before launch; the others estimated from photos). corner: the screen's corner radius in points, iOS's own (UIScreen._displayCornerRadius, github.com/kylebshr/ScreenCorners; the 18 Pro isn't listed there, so the 17 Pro's 62 is assumed). finish: its group in finishes. layout and length: its side buttons and its length in mm; camera: Camera Control's centre in mm (8.55 mm either side of it). Models without a layout use estimatedButtons.",
  "layouts: each button's centre in mm from the phone's top and its half length, from Apple's dimensional drawings (developer.apple.com/accessories, Accessory Design Guidelines). Left: Action button or ring/silent switch, volume up, volume down; right: side button. Apple has no drawings online for the iPhone 11 and older.",
  "estimatedButtons: (left side, top, bottom) as fractions of the band's height, estimated from photos.",
  "finishes: each base colour is AppleDB's for that finish (appledb.dev, deviceFiles/iPhone/<identifier>.json in github.com/littlebyteorg/appledb). band: the band's tone measured from Apple's product photos; without one it is estimated from the base (40% of its light)."
 ],
